# Guo et al. (2025), ApJ 991, 74: "A Search for z=5 Halpha and Hbeta+[OIII] Dual-line Emitting Galaxies in the JWST CEERS Field:
#   Implications for the AGN Abundance"
# arXiv:2409.19205v1 (only arXiv version, submitted), Table 2, "AGN candidates" columns of the UV LF;
#   the AGN-candidate column was checked against Table 2 of the published article and is identical
# Redshift: 5.03 <= z <= 5.26 (set by the F277W+F410M double excess; file at z = 5.1)
# Magnitude definition: M1450 = absolute magnitude at rest-frame 1450 A from a power-law continuum fit to F115W/F150W/F200W/F356W;
#   observed total UV light, no dust correction, no host/AGN decomposition
# Phi convention: log10(Phi / cMpc^-3 mag^-1), 0.5-mag bins, Poisson errors in dex; H0=70, Om=0.3
# Note: "AGN candidates" = the 58 compact (unresolved) Halpha+[OIII] dual-line emitters, ASSUMED to be AGN-dominated; mostly
#   not spectroscopically confirmed (CEERS 2782 is a known broad-line AGN). The "dual-line emitter" columns (mostly star-forming
#   galaxies) are not included.
# Note: Single survey volume (59,340 cMpc^3 over 97 arcmin^2); NO completeness correction applied in the paper.
# Note: The M_UV=-20.5 bin (N=1) is tabulated as an upper limit (<-4.17) and is stored in Guo2025_ulimit.
#
# M1450  LogPhi  UpperDeltaDex  LowerDeltaDex
